              <td class="border border-slate-200 px-3 py-2">₹1,50,000 (₹50,000 where bought for a dependent person with disability), subject to minimum annuity</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="border border-slate-200 px-3 py-2 font-semibold">Entry age</td>
              <td class="border border-slate-200 px-3 py-2">25–85 years (up to 100 for Option F, return of purchase price)</td>
              <td class="border border-slate-200 px-3 py-2">30–79 years; pension (vesting) age 31–80</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="border border-slate-200 px-3 py-2 font-semibold">Annuity options</td>
              <td class="border border-slate-200 px-3 py-2">10 options (A–J) — see section 3</td>
              <td class="border border-slate-200 px-3 py-2">2 options — single life or joint life</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="border border-slate-200 px-3 py-2 font-semibold">Minimum annuity</td>
              <td class="border border-slate-200 px-3 py-2">₹1,000/month, ₹3,000/quarter, ₹6,000/half-year, ₹12,000/year</td>
              <td class="border border-slate-200 px-3 py-2">₹1,000/month, ₹3,000/quarter, ₹6,000/half-year, ₹12,000/year</td>
            </tr>
